      "writtenOn": "2020-02-26T23:28:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Raj,\n\nSorry to exhume an old Comment thread but I\u0027d like more info regarding the following:\n\n\"I think we can keep this solution for now, while we work for the proper solution with the Type-C connector class driver (that will replace extcon driver, on which Benson/Prashant are working on) as applicable.\"\n\nHow is this (the TCSS state synchronization) related to the Type C connector class driver? FWIU based on the patches Heikki sent of his WIP type C connector class driver, I couldn\u0027t see any code about synchronizing TCSS state b/w coreboot and kernel.\n\nCan you detail how a connector class implementation will resolve this issue?\n\nThanks,",
      "parentUuid": "76d511f6_18a5736f",
